{
  "$comment": "Budgets of scripts/bench-browser (npm run bench:browser, CI job browser-bench). Times in ms, heap in MB (after forced garbage collection). The 2,000-block budgets are the product targets (keystroke p95 <= 50, no long task while typing, panel open <= 100, load <= 3 s, bounded heap growth). The 5,000-block budgets allow the larger document: 5,000 blocks is the field's limit. Measured 2026-11-24 on an Apple M3 Pro (Chromium 159 headless, Strapi 5.63, Node 22.23): see CONTRIBUTING.md, Browser benchmark. `enforce: true` fails the CI job; timing budgets are reported in the job summary only, because shared CI runners vary too much for a fixed millisecond limit (see the CI numbers in CONTRIBUTING.md). after-typing-long-task: the longest task in the 1.5 s after the last key, where the field's save and the 2.12 classification of changes since publish run (the unit tests no longer assert time; see tests/helpers/perf-strict.mjs).",
